===Etymology 3===
{{ja-kanjitab|ふみ|y=k|alt=書}}
Possibly a shift from an older {{cog|ltc|-}}-derived reading ''pun''.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref> Earlier Japanese writing was ambiguous regarding the final ''n'' sound spelled {{m|ja|ん}} in modern Japanese, with this sound often spelled (and possibly pronounced) as {{m|ja|む|tr=mu}} instead.

&#42;{{IPAchar|/pumu/}} → {{IPAchar|/pumi/}} → {{IPAchar|/ɸumi/}}

This reading appears in the {{w|Heian period}}, in works such as ''{{w|The Tale of Genji}}''.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref><ref name="DJR">{{R:Daijirin}}</ref>

