===Etymology 2===
{{ja-kanjitab|よき|yomi=k}}
Attested in the ''{{w|Shinsen Jikyō}}'' of {{circa2|898–901 {{CE}}}}, with the ''[[:w:man'yōgana|man'yōgana]]'' spelling {{lang|ja|与支}}.<ref name="KDJ2Yoki">{{R:Nihon Kokugo Daijiten 2 Online|よき 【斧】|lid=200204519316SdRHTZFM|kotobank=斧}}</ref> Presumably from Proto-Japonic, but the first attestation in Japanese is too late to precisely reconstruct the vowels. Cognate with {{cog|jpx-ryu-pro|*yoki}}.

Despite widespread regional attestations, the lack of pitch accent information in standard Japanese could imply that this word is not used in modern standard Japanese.

